      "latex": "\\text{Question: Write a pythagorean triplet whose smallest member is } 8."
    },
    {
      "step_id": "s2",
      "latex": "\\text{Answer: We can get pythagorean triplets by using the general form } 2m, m^2-1, m^2+1."
    },
    {
      "step_id": "s3",
      "latex": "\\text{Let us first take } m^2 - 1 = 8"
    },
    {
      "step_id": "s4",
      "latex": "\\text{so, } m^2 = 8 + 1 = 9"
    },
    {
      "step_id": "s5",
      "latex": "\\text{which gives } m = 3"
    },
    {
      "step_id": "s6",
      "latex": "\\text{Then, } 2m = 6 \\text{ and } m^2 + 1 = 10"
    },
    {
      "step_id": "s7",
      "latex": "\\text{The triplet is thus } 6, 8, 10. \\text{ But } 8 \\text{ is not the smallest member of this.}"
    },
    {
      "step_id": "s8",
      "latex": "\\text{So, let us try } 2m = 8"
    },
    {
      "step_id": "s9",
      "latex": "\\text{then } m = 4"
    },
    {
      "step_id": "s10",
      "latex": "\\text{we get } m^2 - 1 = 16 - 1 = 15"
    },
    {
      "step_id": "s11",
      "latex": "\\text{and } m^2 + 1 = 16 + 1 = 17"
    },
    {
      "step_id": "s12",
      "latex": "\\text{The triplet is } 8, 15, 17 \\text{ with } 8 \\text{ as the smallest member.}"
    },
    {
      "step_id": "s13",
      "latex": "\\text{Note that the member } 8 \\text{ is a power of } 2, \\text{specifically } 2^3 = 8 \\text{ and it is also a composite number.}"
    }
  ],
